    "q-344267": {
      "dom_id": "step-q344267",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+5y=f(x)\n$$\n\non $[-4,4]$, where $f$ is $8$-periodic and odd. Which Fourier-series form is appropriate for a particular solution ${y}_{p}?$$\\,$\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Because $f$ is $8$-periodic on $[-4,4]$, we have $L=4$, so Fourier series on this interval use the basis \n\n$$\ncos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4})\\,\\text{and}\\,sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4}).\n$$\n\nNext, since $f$ is odd, its Fourier series contains only sine terms. For a second-order equation with no ${y}^{′}$ (damping) term, the particular solution inherits this property and is also an odd function.\n\nTherefore, the appropriate form for ${y}_{p}$ is a sine series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{4})\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "select",
          "dom_id": "selectList-344267-0",
          "tag": "custom-select",
